/**
 * Per-ticket memory.
 * A ticket can carry several swaps: the one in the Ticket Tool form plus any the user pastes later.
 * Each gets an entry (numbered once there is more than one); anything resolving to a swap already shown — the same ID again, or that swap's source/destination hash — is ignored.
 *
 * In-memory only: a bot restart forgets every ticket, and recover.js rebuilds them on startup from the bot's own messages.
 */
// ----- Contents (generated by `npm run index` — do not edit) -----
// L34  State
// L42    tickets
// L48    getTicket()
